<title>UK: IMI says buys Wilshire Corp for 24 mln stg.</title>
<headline>IMI says buys Wilshire Corp for 24 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>IMI Plc said on Thursday that it has bought the privately-owned Wilshire Corporation for 24 million stg.</p>
<p>Wilshire is a leading U.S. manufacturer of drinks dispense equipment.  </p>
<p>IMI said the acquisition would be funded from existing bank facilities. The company said the acquisition would enhance its earnings per share in the year to December 31, 1997.</p>
<p>Wilshire employs 400 people and operates three plants in Connecticut, Illinois and Ontario. Its turnover stood at 37 million stg for the year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
